# Docstring coverage (interrogate)

CI (**`devops-ci.yml`** → **`ci-scripts`**) runs **`interrogate scripts -vv --fail-under 95`**, matching **`[tool.interrogate]`** in **`pyproject.toml`** (**`exclude`** includes **`tests/`** — only **`scripts/`** is measured).

When you **add or edit** **`scripts/**/*.py`**, before finishing:

1. Run **`uv run interrogate scripts -vv --fail-under 95`** from the repo root (same as CI). If the **`interrogate`** entrypoint is missing, use **`uv run --group quality-tools python -m interrogate scripts -vv --fail-under 95`** after **`uv sync`**.
2. If it fails, add minimal module/function docstrings until **actual ≥ 95%**; match the style of neighboring modules.

**Always-applied** context: **[`handoff-and-commits.mdc`](handoff-and-commits.mdc)** points here so sessions that touch **`scripts/`** do not skip the gate.

See also **[`python-scripts-ci-gates.mdc`](python-scripts-ci-gates.mdc)** for **pytest** (all green), **line coverage ≥ 95%**, and **pylint ≥ 9.5** on **`scripts/`**.

See also **[`radon-complexity.mdc`](radon-complexity.mdc)** for cyclomatic complexity on **`scripts/`** and **`tests/`**.
